WHAT IS BROKEN, AND WHY IT ONLY BECAME VISIBLE NOW
--------------------------------------------------

`card.prev` arrives in TWO shapes, because the engine keeps two histories and
returns whichever one governs the lift:

  * LEGACY — `rebuild/engine/progression.cjs:134` builds
    `{ d, w, reps:[…], rir, rirSets, debt }`.
  * NATIVE — `progression.cjs:132`, `if (row.native) return row.en;` — the whole
    `earned/performed-lift/v1` entry the app itself recorded. Its per-position
    load and reps sit at `slots[i].fact.current.load.value` and
    `slots[i].fact.current.reps.value` (`rebuild/engine/performed.cjs:225-237`
    reads the same places for `performedLine`).

`gym-model.previousLine()` (gym-model.mjs:142-148 at this tip) tests
`typeof prev.w !== 'number' || !Array.isArray(prev.reps)` and returns `null`
otherwise — i.e. it reads the LEGACY shape only.

Before B-NTC that was harmless: the native shape could not reach this reader,
because a native athlete's second day on a trained lift refused
PERFORMED_NATIVE_TREND_CONTEXT_REQUIRED before any card existed. With the
qualified provider wired (the gym-host.mjs hunk, DECISIONS:108 (b)) and the bind
window on the engine handle, the native record now DOES reach gym-model — delta
cell G6 asserts both of day+3's lifts carry it — and the printed line is still
absent. **The data is there; the reader shape is not.** That is delta cell G7,
and open item O10.

